From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prez2307 <prasiddha@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:07:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] lightbulb F2 checkpoint call sites
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two call sites in agent/tool_executor.py (spec 02 §4.1):

- _dispatch_authorized_once: after scope, pre_tool_call and guardrails,
  before_tool runs inside the start-order step, so a parallel batch acks in
  call order. refuse -> _blocked_tool_result(block_error_type=
  "checkpoint_refused") with state.blocked; replay -> the stored result, no
  dispatch; proceed -> unchanged upstream path.
- _commit_tool_result: after the append and successful session-DB flush,
  tool_committed(ref, persisted_result, effect_disposition) for non-blocked
  calls that passed before_tool (the module tracks them, so skipped,
  abandoned or timed-out slots never commit); an ack failure sets
  _incremental_persistence_failed with cause checkpoint_commit_failed and
  returns None, so the batch stops and the turn ends like a failed flush.
- After a proceed, an interrupt or deadline that landed during the ack
  blocks the call (never dispatched). Replay fires the start callback and,
  on the parallel path, the terminal post_tool_call. The callback runs with
  the turn's ContextVars (propagate_context_to_thread).

With no callback installed a stubbed two-tool turn is identical to the golden
transcript recorded at the pin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
